1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:05,026
Buying with a Clear Purpose An advertisement offered a gorgeous jacket at

2
00:00:05,039 --> 00:00:10,526
a huge discount The material resembled velvet and the lining felt wonderfully

3
00:00:10,539 --> 00:00:15,553
soft I was tempted to buy it immediately although my wardrobe already

4
00:00:15,566 --> 00:00:20,763
contained several similar garments The promise of a bargain had briefly displaced

5
00:00:20,776 --> 00:00:25,263
a more basic question did I need it A consumer can resist

6
00:00:25,276 --> 00:00:31,329
this impulse by considering use quality and total cost An attractive accessory

7
00:00:31,342 --> 00:00:35,697
is not necessarily essential and a fashionable novelty may soon lose its

8
00:00:35,711 --> 00:00:40,316
charm Buying an item in installments does not make it cheaper it

9
00:00:40,329 --> 00:00:45,355
only changes the timing of payment Nor should a complimentary token distract

10
00:00:45,368 --> 00:00:49,553
us from an unreasonable price I left the store and reviewed my

11
00:00:49,566 --> 00:00:54,724
spending The exercise was not about becoming a miser or rejecting every

12
00:00:54,737 --> 00:01:01,355
pleasure It was about ensuring that consumption reflected my priorities I eventually

13
00:01:01,368 --> 00:01:05,171
bought a sturdy coat that I could mend easily Had I followed

14
00:01:05,184 --> 00:01:10,132
the initial excitement I would have purchased something less suitable A deliberate

15
00:01:10,145 --> 00:01:14,132
pause can transform shopping from a reflex into a considered choice
